<article class="resource-hub">
  <header class="hub-header">
    <h1>Where to Buy Cannabis Seeds in Maine 2026</h1>
    <p class="lead">A curated directory of Maine-licensed dispensaries carrying seeds, online seed banks that ship to Maine, and Maine-licensed clone producers. Plus the legal framework for buying cannabis seeds in Maine as an adult 21+, and what to look for in a Maine-adapted genetic.</p>
    <div class="byline">
      <p><strong>By Margaret Finch</strong> · Maine Dispensary Guide editorial team</p>
      <p class="last-updated">Published 2026-07-23 · Last reviewed 2026-07-23</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="answer-capsule">
    <strong>Short answer:</strong> You can buy cannabis seeds in Maine three ways: (1) at Maine-licensed adult-use dispensaries (in-person, with a 21+ ID), (2) from online seed banks that ship to Maine (ILGM, MSNL, Seed Connect, Humboldt Seed Company, Royal Queen Seeds, Dutch Passion), or (3) from Maine-licensed clone producers for head-start seedlings. Federal law treats cannabis seeds as marijuana under the Controlled Substances Act, so interstate shipping exists in a legal gray area; in-state dispensary purchases are the cleanest legal path.
  </div>

  <section class="resource-sections">

    <div class="resource-section">
      <h2>1. Maine-licensed dispensaries carrying seeds</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Buying in-state at a licensed dispensary is the cleanest legal path for Maine residents. The dispensary is licensed by the Office of Cannabis Policy and the seeds are sold under that license. Inventory varies by location and season — call ahead. The list below is curated from public dispensary menus and operator websites; verify current inventory before driving.</p>

      <div class="resource-card">
        <h3>Cannabis Seed Bank of Maine</h3>
        <div class="resource-meta">Farmington, ME · In-person</div>
        <p>Maine-based retail seed shop operating in the Farmington area. Curated genetics with a Maine-adapted focus. Carries both autoflower and photoperiod seeds from multiple breeders.</p>
        <p><a href="https://cannabisseedbankofmaine.com" class="resource-link" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">cannabisseedbankofmaine.com</a></p>
        <div class="resource-note">Operating hours, current address, and breeder list change frequently; check the website or call before visiting. Maine Dispensary Guide does not have a commercial relationship with this vendor.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="resource-card">
        <h3>Seed &amp; Soil Maine</h3>
        <div class="resource-meta">Monroe, ME · In-person + online</div>
        <p>Maine-based seed retailer and Humboldt Seed Company affiliate. Carries Humboldt's full catalog with a 90% germination guarantee. Strong cold-climate selection suited to Maine's compressed season.</p>
        <p><a href="https://seedandsoilmaine.com" class="resource-link" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">seedandsoilmaine.com</a></p>
        <div class="resource-note">Public Humboldt Seed Company affiliate program; affiliate relationship terms not independently verified by Maine Dispensary Guide.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="resource-card">
        <h3>North Atlantic Seed Co.</h3>
        <div class="resource-meta">Waterville, ME · Wholesale + retail</div>
        <p>Maine-licensed cannabis seed producer. Wholesale and retail bulk packs. Carries their own in-house genetics as well as distributed lines. Useful for buyers looking to plant a larger outdoor run and buy in bulk.</p>
        <p><a href="https://northatlanticseed.com" class="resource-link" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">northatlanticseed.com</a></p>
        <div class="resource-note">Bulk and wholesale pricing requires direct contact; retail pricing available on the website catalog.</div>
      </div>

      <Callout title="Maine dispensaries vary on seed inventory" type="info">
        Most licensed adult-use dispensaries in Maine do NOT carry seeds — they sell flower, concentrates, edibles, and pre-rolls. A small subset carries seeds; expect a call-ahead or a dedicated seed-bank visit. For clone starts, see Section 3 below.
      </Callout>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-section">
      <h2>2. Online seed banks that ship to Maine</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Cannabis seeds occupy a contested legal position: under federal law (Controlled Substances Act), cannabis seeds are marijuana. Most reputable seed banks operate from outside the U.S. (Netherlands, Spain, UK) and ship internationally in a manner they characterize as "novelty" or "souvenir" sales. The risk falls on the buyer at the customs border. Maine residents have ordered from these banks for years with no documented enforcement, but the risk is real.</p>
      <Callout title="Federal legal status" type="warning">
        As of this writing (2026-07-23), cannabis seeds are federally classified as marijuana under the Controlled Substances Act. The U.S. Postal Service will seize packages containing cannabis seeds. Private carriers (UPS, FedEx) generally do not, but packages can still be intercepted. The November 2025 federal hemp definition change has not yet reclassified high-THC seeds as of this writing. Verify current federal status before ordering.
      </Callout>

