    <div class="resource-section">
      <h2>3. Maine-licensed clone producers</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Clones (cuttings) give Maine growers a head start on the season — typically 4–6 weeks of growth — which is a real advantage in a 110–160 day outdoor window. Maine-licensed clone producers operate under the medical caregiver framework and may have specific intake requirements.</p>

      <div class="resource-card">
        <h3>Maine Clone Company</h3>
        <div class="resource-meta">Waterville, ME · Medical caregiver model</div>
        <p>Maine-licensed clone producer operating under the medical caregiver framework. Carries established clones of popular photoperiod and autoflower varieties, with documented mother-plant lineage. Head-start clones that save 4–6 weeks of vegetation time.</p>
        <p><a href="https://maineclonecompany.com" class="resource-link" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">maineclonecompany.com</a></p>
