    <div class="resource-section">
      <h2>4. The legal framework for buying cannabis seeds in Maine</h2>
      <p>Buying seeds as an adult 21+ in Maine is legal under the personal cultivation framework. What you do with them matters:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Plant count limit:</strong> Six mature / twelve immature / unlimited seedlings per adult 21+ (28-B M.R.S. §1502 as amended by P.L. 2023 c. 220)</li>
        <li><strong>Tagging requirement:</strong> Each plant must have a legible tag with the cultivator's name, license/registration number (if applicable), and a plant identifier</li>
        <li><strong>Location rules:</strong> Cultivation must be on land the adult owns or is domiciled on, or with written owner permission. The site must not be visible from a public way without aid of binoculars or aircraft, and must be secured against access by anyone under 21</li>
        <li><strong>No sale:</strong> You may not sell cannabis, including seeds you germinated, to anyone except a licensed caregiver, dispensary, or via a registered caregiver-to-licensee transfer. Gifting is also regulated</li>
        <li><strong>Transport:</strong> Seeds and finished cannabis may be transported in a sealed container in your vehicle, but the container must be inaccessible to the driver and passengers (i.e., the trunk is the safest interpretation)</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="source-note">Source: 28-B M.R.S. §1502; 28-B M.R.S. §1501 (possession); Maine OCP consumer FAQ. The Maine home grow guide on Maine Dispensary Guide has the full text of §1502 with annotations.</p>
    </div>

